Here's how to accomplish this task:

1. First, let's fetch the posts by user ID 3 using the `http-get` tool. We'll make a GET request to `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts?userId=3` to get the posts data.

2. Next, we need to enrich each post with its comment count. We can do this by making another GET request to `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/{postId}/comments` for each post ID, and then counting the number of comments.

3. Finally, we'll write the enriched posts data to a TypeScript module file (`output.ts`) using the `file-write` tool.

Here's the code that will be written to `output.ts`:

```typescript
// Define the interface for a Post
interface Post {
    userId: number;
    id: number;
    title: string;
    body: string;
}

// Define the interface for a Comment
interface Comment {
    postId: number;
    id: number;
    name: string;
    email: string;
    body: string;
}

// Define the interface for an EnrichedPost
interface EnrichedPost {
    userId: number;
    id: number;
    title: string;
    body: string;
    commentCount: number;
}

// Fetch posts by user ID 3
const postsResponse = await http-get('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts?userId=3');

// Parse the posts response
const posts: Post[] = JSON.parse(postsResponse.content);

// Enrich each post with its comment count
const enrichedPosts: EnrichedPost[] = posts.map(post => {
    // Fetch comments for this post
    const commentsResponse = await http-get(`https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${post.id}/comments`);
    const comments: Comment[] = JSON.parse(commentsResponse.content);

    // Calculate comment count
    const commentCount = comments.length;

    // Return enriched post
    return {
        userId: post.userId,
        id: post.id,
        title: post.title,
        body: post.body,
        commentCount: commentCount
    };
});

// Export the enriched posts as a constant
export const EnrichedPosts = enrichedPosts;
```

